# Sample Vite production profile for Heavy-Rental/heavy-rental-react-web-portal
# Copy to the React repo as `.env.production` (Vite name — not `.env.prod`).
#
# This is a React + TypeScript + Vite SPA built with npm (`npm ci`, `npm run build`).
# Vite inlines import.meta.env.VITE_* at build time. nginx does not read this file.
# Release seeds/scans this file, then `npx tsc -b && npx vite build --mode api`
# so import.meta.env.MODE === "api" (Spring login / cart / deposit). Process env
# still wins and empties VITE_API_TARGET (do not bake http://heavy-rental-rest-api:8080).
# Do NOT COPY this file into the nginx image (ADR 0007). CD does not read it.
#
# Spring REST (heavy-rental-spring-rest-api) owns browser-facing /api on :8080.
# Haystack is private (REST → Haystack). The SPA must not call Haystack.
#
# Ownership (infra aws-infra-academy.yml → sync-secrets):
#   Terraform ALBs → heavy-rental/portal REST_BASE_URL=http://<rest_alb>:8080
#   Infra academy Stripe secrets → portal SM pk_ only
#   REST SM also gets APP_CORS=http://<portal_alb>, HAYSTACK_BASE_URL, sk_/whsec_, JWT, RDS
#   Portal CD mounts guest nginx /api → REST_BASE_URL (process is the proxy, not VITE_*)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same-origin /api (Release forces these empty on `npm run build`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_API_URL=
VITE_REST_URL=
VITE_REST_BASE_URL=
VITE_HAYSTACK_URL=
VITE_HAYSTACK_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# From AWS — do not set here
# REST_BASE_URL          Terraform rest_alb_dns → heavy-rental/portal (CD /api)
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY infra academy secret → portal SM (and REST SM)
# STRIPE_API_KEY / STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET  REST only (sk_ / whsec_)
# APP_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS  Terraform portal_alb_dns → REST SM (not the SPA)
# HAYSTACK_BASE_URL      Terraform haystack_alb_dns → REST SM (not the SPA)
# POSTGRES_* / APP_JWT_SECRET / ONEMAP_* / DYNAMIC_PRICING_* / PRICING_*
#                        REST (and Haystack) only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REST_BASE_URL=
# STRIPE_API_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# APP_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# HAYSTACK_BASE_URL=
# POSTGRES_HOSTNAME=
# APP_JWT_SECRET=

# Stripe pk_: set GitHub Environment academy variable VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
# Release injects it at vite build --mode api. Do not commit a real pk_ here.
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
